-- חוזר הממונה על השכר 2025-1-8 — תוספת מעונות (זכויות הוריות), עדכון התוספת (19.1.2025)
-- The Wage Controller updates the monthly childcare supplement (parental
-- rights) for a child up to age 5 by the change in the index, under clause
-- 11 of the framework agreement of 12.1.2011, and prints the new amounts.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT common

§ `תוספת מעונות (זכויות הוריות), עדכון התוספת`

-- akn:hc_1/p1 akn:hc_1/p2 akn:hc_1/p3 akn:hc_1/p4 akn:hc_1/p5 The date, the circular's number, the addressees (the Deputy Accountant-General and the public-sector employers) and the subject line; no rule.

@desc A child for whom the childcare supplement is claimed, as far as this circular asks about it.
DECLARE `child for the childcare supplement` HAS
    `up to age 5`                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc the child is "עד גיל 5", the age the circular names; who that is, and who may claim, is clause 11 of the framework agreement of 12.1.2011, which this circular does not restate
    `place among the children`      IS A NUMBER  @desc 1 for "ילד אחד / ילד ראשון" (an only or first child), 2 for "ילד שני" (a second child), counted as clause 11 of the framework agreement counts them

§§ `The update`

-- The date and the index change as printed. F-2025-01-19_sachar_2025-1-8_maonot-a:
-- the date is 1.1.2024, the day the previous year's update took effect at
-- other amounts; it is encoded as printed, because this file encodes this
-- circular's own words. (Circular 2025-1-12 of 5.2.2025 reprints the same
-- update from 1.1.2025 as a "clerical-error correction"; its own file
-- carries that date.)
@ref akn:hc_1/p6
`the update takes effect` MEANS Date 1 1 2024

@ref akn:hc_1/p6
`the change in the index` MEANS 3.24%

-- "בהתאם לשיעור השינוי במדד": the supplement moves by the index change. The
-- circular names neither the amount before the update nor a rounding; it
-- prints the result, in whole shekels, below.
@ref akn:hc_1/p6
GIVEN `the amount before the update` IS A NUMBER @desc the supplement's amount in force before this update, set by the previous year's circular; not printed here
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the amount moved by the index` `the amount before the update` IS
    `the amount before the update` TIMES (1 PLUS `the change in the index`)

§§ `1–2 The amounts`

@ref akn:hc_1__para_1
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly amount for an only or first child` IS 362

@ref akn:hc_1__para_2
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly amount for a second child` IS 245

-- The circular prints amounts for an only or first child and for a second
-- child, and nothing for any other: whether a third child is paid for is
-- the framework agreement's question, not this circular's, so this circular
-- gives NOTHING there rather than a zero it does not print.
@export default The monthly childcare supplement (in shekels) this update sets for a child, from the date it takes effect
@ref akn:hc_1/p6
GIVEN c       IS A `child for the childcare supplement` @desc the child
      `month` IS A DATE                                @desc a day in the month the supplement is for
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` c `month` IS
    BRANCH IF `month` LESS THAN `the update takes effect` THEN NOTHING
           IF (NOT c's `up to age 5`)                    THEN NOTHING
           IF c's `place among the children` EQUALS 1   THEN JUST `the monthly amount for an only or first child`
           IF c's `place among the children` EQUALS 2   THEN JUST `the monthly amount for a second child`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Payment`

DECLARE `childcare supplement action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the childcare supplement` HAS `childcare amount paid` IS A NUMBER

-- The circular is addressed to the public-sector employers: from the date
-- it takes effect they pay the supplement at the updated amount. It sets a
-- monthly amount ("לחודש") and no payment date; time here is counted in
-- months from the start of the month the supplement is for, and the
-- supplement is read as due within that month.
@ref akn:hc_1/p6 akn:hc_1__para_1 akn:hc_1__para_2
GIVEN c       IS A `child for the childcare supplement`
      `month` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `childcare supplement action`
DECIDE `the employer pays the updated supplement` c `month` IS
    CONSIDER `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` c `month`
    WHEN JUST due THEN
        PARTY `the employer`
        MUST  `pay the childcare supplement` paid
              PROVIDED paid AT LEAST due
        WITHIN 1
        LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "the childcare supplement was not paid at the updated amount for the month"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FULFILLED

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off (the Wage Controller) and the copy to the acting Civil Service Commissioner; no rule.

§§ `Findings`

-- F-2025-01-19_sachar_2025-1-8_maonot-a. The amounts in force from 1.1.2024
-- as circular 2024-1-7 of 31.1.2024 prints them (corpus
-- circulars-sachar/2024-01_sachar_2024-1-7_maonot, ¶¶1–2): 351 and 237.
-- They are used here only as evidence, never as a rule of this circular.
`the 2024 circular's amount for an only or first child` MEANS 351
`the 2024 circular's amount for a second child`         MEANS 237
`the 2024 circular's effective date`                    MEANS Date 1 1 2024

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `within half a shekel of` x y IF
        x AT LEAST y MINUS 0.5
    AND x AT MOST y PLUS 0.5

-- This circular's amounts are the 2024 amounts moved once more by its own
-- 3.24% (351 → 362.37, 237 → 244.68), i.e. the update that follows the one
-- of 1.1.2024; and yet it dates them from 1.1.2024, the date on which the
-- 2024 circular set 351 and 237. For January 2024 the two circulars give
-- two different amounts.
`the update is dated to the day the previous update took effect at other amounts` MEANS
        `the update takes effect` EQUALS `the 2024 circular's effective date`
    AND (NOT (`the monthly amount for an only or first child` EQUALS `the 2024 circular's amount for an only or first child`))
    AND `within half a shekel of` `the monthly amount for an only or first child` (`the amount moved by the index` `the 2024 circular's amount for an only or first child`)
    AND `within half a shekel of` `the monthly amount for a second child` (`the amount moved by the index` `the 2024 circular's amount for a second child`)
#ASSERT `the update is dated to the day the previous update took effect at other amounts`

§§ `Examples`

`an only child of three` MEANS
    `child for the childcare supplement` WITH
        `up to age 5`              IS TRUE
        `place among the children` IS 1

`a second child of two` MEANS
    `child for the childcare supplement` WITH
        `up to age 5`              IS TRUE
        `place among the children` IS 2

`a third child of one` MEANS
    `child for the childcare supplement` WITH
        `up to age 5`              IS TRUE
        `place among the children` IS 3

`a first child of seven` MEANS
    `child for the childcare supplement` WITH
        `up to age 5`              IS FALSE
        `place among the children` IS 1

#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` `an only child of three` (Date 1 1 2024) EQUALS JUST 362
#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` `a second child of two` (Date 15 3 2025) EQUALS JUST 245
#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` `an only child of three` (Date 31 12 2023) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` `a third child of one` (Date 1 2 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` `a first child of seven` (Date 1 2 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#EVAL   `the amount moved by the index` 100

-- Paid in full within the month, the obligation is fulfilled; paid short,
-- it is still owed.
#TRACE `the employer pays the updated supplement` `an only child of three` (Date 1 2 2025) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the childcare supplement` 362 AT 0
#TRACE `the employer pays the updated supplement` `an only child of three` (Date 1 2 2025) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the childcare supplement` 300 AT 0
